      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As a professional ui/ux designer of eight years, Here's how you fix it;\n\nRollback the original avatar menu.\n\nMove the new Avatar Market component to the Marketplace tab, where it should've been to start with, for a consistent and intuitive storefront.\n\nSpecific feedback;\n\nThe new avatar menu pane design fails basic ux design on several counts;\n\nIt's inconsistent with the rest of the client app.\n\nIt prioritizes browsing, and assigns the largest button to Details over Applying an avatar for a purchase-focused layout and makes it harder to apply avatars because it's a secondary button.  This is bad design when the primary use-case should ALWAYS be the user applying owned avatars.\n\nThe tick doesn't infer what it does at a glance vs \"Apply\".  Position should also  be swapped with the Details button, which can be inferred by using the avatar quality icons instead of text for visual shorthand of the details tab and the avatar's rating itself.\n\nNone of these changes should require major code changes that may break a build, only moving existing component placement in the UI layout and icon change on existing buttons.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
